# Commit and PR helper policy

When the user asks to create a git commit in this repository:

- Prefer `scripts/git-commit-with-models.sh` over raw `git commit`.
- Ask for commit subject/body only if missing.
- Use `--subject` for the commit title.
- If there is a body file or text, pass it with `--body`.
- Keep normal git safety behavior (no destructive git commands, no force push unless explicitly requested).

When the user asks to create a pull request in this repository:

- Prefer `scripts/gh-pr-create-with-models.sh` so the PR body includes model usage details.
- Ask for title/body/base only if missing.
- Pass extra PR flags through to the helper script.

If the user explicitly asks to bypass these helpers, follow the user request.
